        <item>
            <title>0.2.5</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:56:53 -0400</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.2.5</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2.5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>12.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<pre>VisiDAW 0.2.5

Signed universal macOS release for Apple Silicon and Intel, targeting macOS 12 or later.

This release uses the STABLE Sparkle update feed and production Polar licensing. A valid VisiDAW license and an internet connection are required for initial activation; an accepted saved activation supports offline use. Existing production activations retain the same licensing identity.

Includes the standard Sparkle update interface and the shared save/quit handling used by normal quit and update installation. TESTING installations remain on their own feed; install this STABLE app to use the customer update channel.

Phone/WebRTC recording and MP4 export remain experimental.

FFmpeg/FFprobe corresponding source and build recipe:
https://github.com/jacobpark1919/visidaw-updates/releases/download/ffmpeg-source-8.1.2-macos-universal/VisiDAW-FFmpeg-8.1.2-macos-universal-source.tar.xz
Source SHA-256: 203172291b93231ac8b5dc6ae7ef58844fa0b0c8ffb4aba4c60065a539e0c885

This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group. Component license texts and notices are included with the app and source archive.
</pre>]]></description>
